@startuml geo-cell-write
title US-12: Geo-Cell Write - Historical index + live Redis spatial membership

skinparam sequenceArrowThickness 1.5
skinparam participantBorderColor #555555
skinparam participantBackgroundColor #F8F8F8
skinparam noteBorderColor #AAAAAA
skinparam noteBackgroundColor #FFFDE7

queue "Kafka\nadsb.raw / ais.raw" as Kafka
participant "Position\nConsumer" as Consumer
database "TimescaleDB\nposition_history" as TSDB
database "Redis\nentity:live:{id}" as Live
database "Redis\ngeo-cell:{cell}\n(sorted sets)" as GeoCell

Kafka -> Consumer : consume event\n{ entity_id, lat, lon, timestamp_ms }
Consumer -> Consumer : compute history_geo_cell\nand live_geo_cell

Consumer -> Live : HGET last_seen_ms, live_geo_cell
Live --> Consumer : previous timestamp + previous live cell

alt incoming.timestamp_ms < stored.last_seen_ms
  note over Consumer
    Stale/out-of-order event.
    Do not regress live hash or geo-cell membership.
    Historical TimescaleDB insert remains independently idempotent.
  end note
else current/newer event
  Consumer -> TSDB : INSERT position_history\ngeo_cell = history_geo_cell\nON CONFLICT DO NOTHING

  alt previous live cell exists AND changed
    Consumer -> GeoCell : ZREM geo-cell:{old_cell} entity_id
  end

  Consumer -> GeoCell : ZADD geo-cell:{live_geo_cell}\ntimestamp_ms entity_id
  Consumer -> Live : HSET latest position + last_seen_ms\n+ live_geo_cell; refresh safety TTL
end

note over TSDB
  TimescaleDB partitions by observed_at only.
  history_geo_cell is an indexed query column,
  not a chunk/partition dimension.
end note

note over GeoCell
  score = last_seen_ms
  Correlation Worker uses ZRANGEBYSCORE
  over nearby LIVE_H3_RESOLUTION cells,
  then performs exact distance checks.
end note

@enduml
